that get uploaded every day.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:39.330
So that's where the upload
functionality comes in.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:43.770
Now, the next important part
is the intelligent extraction

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:45.231
of these invoices.

00:19:45.231 --> 00:19:47.730
So you have got these invoices
which are uploaded and ready.

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:50.670
How do you actually understand
the information there?

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:55.620
And there are again three
steps to this intelligent text

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:57.180
extraction.

00:19:57.180 --> 00:20:01.860
Step number one is
using the Vision API

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:06.360
to actually extract the
detail from the invoice.

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:09.030
So, for that they are
using Google's machine

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:10.140
learning Vision API.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.110
Extremely capable
API tool there.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:16.620
We have seen it work with
different kinds of invoices.

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:19.650
I mean, invoices often
have scribbled text--

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.180
text manually written.

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:24.480
All those kind of invoices
also work extremely well

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:25.920
with the Vision API.

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:30.480
Then the next component is now
you have extracted the details.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:32.890
How do you know what
information is where?

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:36.750
So for that, we have
YAML config which

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:39.420
comes into play, which
helps us in understanding

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:42.090
what information is
read in the invoice.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.980
So that's step number two.

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:47.520
Now the third thing is you
have extracted the information.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:51.960
How do you know that
this particular invoice

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:54.990
is a template from
a particular vendor.

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:56.440
How do you connect this?

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:59.490
That's where the third
component, which is AutoML,

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:00.780
comes in.

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:03.390
And then we developed
the solution--

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:07.140
we've been developing that
over a period of time.

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:11.160
We had used traditional ML
and we also used AutoML.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.200
And once we started
using AutoML,

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:16.830
we actually saw that there was
a good increase in confidence

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.010
per sent page.

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:19.590
So when I show you
the demo, you'd

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:22.050
actually get a peek at it.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:26.530
But with AutoML, we were really
able to enhance the solution.

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:29.250
So the combination of
these three-- extraction

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:32.430
of the solution and
then classification

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:35.340
of the solution-- you're
actually able to do

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:37.650
